<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Bahrain</h1><p class="st-meta">1971 CE – present · capital Manama</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Independent Bahrain since 1971, a Gulf financial centre ruled by the Al Khalifa and a kingdom since 2002.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> mission found that Bahrainis wanted independence rather than union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> ended its protection of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Sheikhdom of Bahrain</a>, and the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> became independent on 15 August 1971 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isa-bin-salman-al-khalifa">Isa bin Salman Al Khalifa</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>An elected parliament created by the constitution of 1973 was dissolved in 1975. With modest oil reserves, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> built an offshore banking sector, aluminium smelting and a causeway to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>, opened in 1986, and hosts the US Fifth Fleet. Tension between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> ruling family and the Shi'a majority produced unrest in the 1990s. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamad-bin-isa-al-khalifa">Hamad bin Isa</a>, ruler from 1999, introduced a National Action Charter and proclaimed a kingdom in 2002.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>In 2011 mass protests at the Pearl Roundabout were suppressed with the help of Saudi and Emirati forces. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> remains a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> with strong royal power; it normalised relations with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Israel</a> in 2020.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-bahrain.jpg" alt="State of Bahrain" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Hoshie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bahrain_(1972%E2%80%932002).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1971 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Manama</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Isa bin Salman Al Khalifa, Hamad bin Isa Al Khalifa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam (Shi'a majority, Sunni rulers)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bahrain">Bahrain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Bahrain, Bahrain</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1998&amp;focus=state-of-bahrain" aria-label="State of Bahrain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6015 1220 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of Bahrain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6335 1476L6335 1476"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6335 1476h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6335 1476h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6335 1476h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1998&amp;focus=state-of-bahrain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
